{'symbol': 'REGN', 'date': '2021-05-21 11:45:00', 'title': 'TEEN SCIENTISTS AND ENGINEERS WIN $5 MILLION AT LARGEST GLOBAL HIGH SCHOOL STEM COMPETITION', 'text': "TARRYTOWN, N.Y.\xa0AND\xa0WASHINGTON, MAY 21, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- $75,000 TOP AWARD GOES TO 16-YEAR-OLD MICHELLE HUA FOR NOVEL HUMAN ACTION RECOGNITION ALGORITHM IN REGENERON INTERNATIONAL SCIENCE AND ENGINEERING FAIR 2021 REGENERON PHARMACEUTICALS, INC. \xa0(NASDAQ: REGN) AND SOCIETY FOR SCIENCE \xa0(THE SOCIETY) ANNOUNCED THAT MICHELLE HUA, 16, OF TROY, MICHIGAN, WON THE $75,000 TOP AWARD IN THE 2021 REGENERON INTERNATIONAL SCIENCE AND ENGINEERING FAIR (REGENERON ISEF), THE WORLD'S LARGEST GLOBAL HIGH SCHOOL COMPETITION."}